 kw="Coastal Cabana renovation, Coastal Cabana interior design, Coastal Cabana floor plan, Loyang EC renovation, Coastal Cabana built-in carpentry, Jalan Loyang Besar interior design",
 cite=[CC_SITE, CC_BRO, CC_DEV],
 ts={
  "3brd":("3-Bedroom Deluxe","The most compact type here, so storage has to sit along whole walls. An entry cabinet, a slim TV and display wall and a kitchen run with a tall pantry column keep the living area open. Full-height wardrobes in all three bedrooms, with a fold-down desk in one, carry most families.",["Entry shoe cabinet","Kitchen run with a tall pantry or fridge column","Full-height wardrobes in every bedroom"],["Fold-down desk in a common bedroom","Dining bench with drawers"],_ECM),
  "3brp":("3-Bedroom Premium","The extra space over the Deluxe suits a defined dining zone and a longer living-room storage wall. In the Premium + Study type, plan the study as a real work room: a wall-to-wall desk, shelving above and good task light, so it does not end up as a store room.",["Entry cabinet and a living-room storage wall","Kitchen run with a pantry column","Wardrobes in every bedroom"],["A built-in desk and shelving in the study","Platform bed with drawers in the master bedroom"],_ECM),
  "4brc":("4-Bedroom Classic","Four bedrooms in 92 sq m means every room needs storage that does not eat floor space. Use full-height wardrobes with sliding doors where swing space is tight, a platform bed with drawers in the smaller rooms and a compact desk in one common bedroom.",["Full-height wardrobes in all four bedrooms","Entry cabinet","Kitchen run with a tall pantry column"],["Sliding wardrobe doors in the smaller rooms","Platform beds with drawers"],_ECM),
  "4brd":("4-Bedroom Deluxe","The Type D2 plan has a living room that opens to a balcony, dining inward toward a compact kitchen and yard, a corner master with its own bath and three common bedrooms. Most owners ask for a living-room storage wall, a fitted kitchen with a tall pantry run, a master wardrobe wall and a built-in desk in one common bedroom.",["Fitted kitchen with a tall pantry or fridge run","Full-height wardrobes in all four bedrooms","Entry cabinet and a living-room storage wall","Laundry cabinet in the yard"],["Built-in dining bench","Platform bed with drawers in the master bedroom","Wall-to-wall study desk in a common bedroom"],["Ordering furniture before you have the approved plan","Planning balcony screens or grilles without MCST approval","Tall units placed where doors cannot open fully"]),
  "4brp":("4-Bedroom Premium","The larger 4-bedroom types add space, and in the Study and Flexi versions an extra room. Decide early what the study or flexi room is for, a home office, a helper's room or a guest room, because that sets its joinery, power points and lighting.",["Wardrobes in every bedroom","Kitchen run with a pantry column","A clear brief for the study or flexi room"],["A dressing counter in the master bedroom","A built-in desk wall in the study"],_ECM),
  "5brp":("5-Bedroom Premium","The largest homes here suit a multi-generation family. Plan who sleeps where first, keep routes to the bathrooms wide, and give every bedroom a full-height wardrobe so shared spaces stay clear. A long feature wall in the living area can carry both display and closed storage.",["Wardrobes in every bedroom","Entry shoe and bag cabinet","Wide routes between bedrooms and bathrooms"],["A study corner visible from the living area","Shared storage near the entry"],["Planning bedrooms before agreeing who sleeps where","Narrow corridors that block a walking aid"]),
 },
 theory={"Kitchen":"A compact condo kitchen works when every surface earns its place. One continuous run keeps the working triangle short, a tall pantry column takes the bulk storage off the counter, and lit niches or a lit shelf give light where the work happens. A single colour on the doors keeps a small room from feeling cut up."},
 types=[("3-Bedroom Deluxe","3brd","Types C1a and C1b: 46 homes, 81 sq m (872 sq ft)"),("3-Bedroom Premium","3brp","Type C2: 139 homes, 85 sq m (915 sq ft). Premium + Study Type C3: 165 homes, 85 sq m (915 sq ft)"),("4-Bedroom Classic","4brc","Type D1: 59 homes, 92 sq m (990 sq ft)"),("4-Bedroom Deluxe","4brd","Type D2: 142 homes, 94 sq m (1,012 sq ft)"),("4-Bedroom Premium","4brp","Type D3: 59 homes, 98 sq m (1,055 sq ft). Premium + Study D4 and D4-B: 68 homes, 108 or 113 sq m (1,163 or 1,216 sq ft). Premium + Flexi D5: 48 homes, 112 sq m (1,206 sq ft)"),("5-Bedroom Premium","5brp","Types E1 and E2: 22 homes, 127 or 132 sq m (1,367 or 1,421 sq ft)")],
 glance=[("Type","Executive condominium, District 17"),("Developer","Pasir Ris Development Pte. Ltd. (UEN 202436619N, developer licence C1530), jointly developed by Qingjian Realty (South Pacific) Group, Forsea Holdings, ZACD and Jianan Capital"),("Address","Blocks 2 to 32 (even numbers) Jalan Loyang Besar, MK31 Lot 05452V"),("Units","748 homes in 16 residential blocks: Blocks 2, 4, 6 and 8 of 11 storeys, Blocks 10 to 32 of 12 storeys"),("Tenure","99 years from 13 November 2024"),("Expected dates","Vacant possession 31 March 2029, legal completion 31 March 2032, as published by the developer. Not a key appointment"),("Launch date","Not stated on the official website or in the brochure")],
 plans=[dict(img="coastal-cabana-brochure-type-d2-4-bedroom-deluxe.webp",w=2000,h=3111,alt="Official Coastal Cabana brochure floor plans of 4-Bedroom Deluxe Type D2 and first-storey Type D2 (p), 94 square metres (1,012 square feet)",title="4-Bedroom Deluxe Type D2, 94 sq m (1,012 sq ft)",cap="Typical floors in Blocks 4, 16, 18, 22, 28 and 32, mirrored in Blocks 2, 14, 20, 24, 26 and 30. The living room opens to a balcony, dining sits inward toward a compact kitchen and yard with an adjacent household shelter, the corner master bedroom has its own bath, and Bedrooms 2, 3 and 4 are the common rooms. The same sheet shows the first-storey Type D2 (p), with a private enclosed space in place of the balcony. Area includes balcony or PES; AC and RC ledges are excluded. A type plan, not a specific stack.",credit="Floor plan: Coastal Cabana brochure, page 30, Pasir Ris Development Pte. Ltd.",curl=CC_BRO)],
 plan_gaps="This is the developer's Type D2 plan, the most common 4-bedroom type (142 of 748 homes), not a specific stack. The brochure says areas are approximate, not to scale and subject to final survey, and plans can be amended by the building authorities. Plans for the other 3-, 4- and 5-bedroom types are in the same brochure (pages 28 to 33). We do not assume a sea view for any stack.",
 oth_txt="The official plan for this type is in the developer's brochure, pages 28 to 33.",
 keep1="Keep: the household shelter walls next to the yard. They must not be hacked or drilled.",
 keep2="Check first: any other wall, and anything seen from outside. We confirm with your approved plan, the condo by-laws and MCST approval before we quote.",
 rooms4=dict(
  living="The living room opens to a balcony, with dining set further in toward the kitchen. Put the TV and storage wall on the solid living wall, keep the line to the balcony door clear, and give the dining bench the wall nearest the kitchen. Check the condo rules before you plan balcony screens or outdoor cabinets.",
  kitchen="The kitchen is compact and opens to a yard, with the household shelter alongside. One continuous run with a tall fridge and pantry column keeps the floor free, and a laundry cabinet in the yard takes washing out of the kitchen.",
  main="The master bedroom sits at the corner with its own bath. A recessed bed-head wall with lit niches, a platform bed with drawers and a full-height wardrobe on the longest wall keep the window side open.",
  common="Bedrooms 2, 3 and 4 are the common rooms. Give each a full-height wardrobe, and plan one as a study with a wall-to-wall desk and knee space, so the home works for a growing family.",
  other="The common bath serves the three common bedrooms and guests. Plan a vanity cabinet, a mirror cabinet and niches. Any change to wet-area finishes needs MCST approval first."),
 feat=dict(living="the Type D2 living room that opens to a balcony",kitchen="the compact Type D2 kitchen that opens to a yard",main="the corner master bedroom with its own bath",common="one of the three common bedrooms in Type D2"),
 renders=[
  R("Living room","Amber Slat Teak Living","living-amber-slat-teak-living","42% 50%","A full-height amber-stained slatted teak TV wall with cove lighting and a floating console, and a built-in dining bench on the kitchen side, with the living opening to a balcony. Window view illustrative.","Amber Slat Teak Living room concept for a Coastal Cabana 4-Bedroom Deluxe Type D2 with an amber slatted teak TV wall, floating console, built-in dining bench and a balcony"),
  R("Kitchen","Ochre Clay Galley Kitchen","kitchen-ochre-clay-galley-kitchen","42% 50%","Ochre-clay inset-panel cabinets with brass knobs, a warm quartz counter and full-height backsplash, and under-cabinet lighting, sized for the compact Type D2 kitchen that opens to a yard.","Ochre Clay Galley Kitchen detail for Coastal Cabana with ochre-clay inset-panel cabinets, brass knobs, a warm quartz counter and backsplash, and under-cabinet lighting"),
  R("Main bedroom","Tobacco Hide Night Suite","main-bedroom-tobacco-hide-night-suite","50% 48%","A recessed tobacco-leather headboard wall with lit bedside niches, a built-in platform bed, and a full-height walnut wardrobe with bronze-tinted glass doors. Evening view illustrative.","Tobacco Hide Night Suite main bedroom concept for Coastal Cabana with a full-width recessed tobacco-leather headboard, lit bedside niches, platform bed and a walnut glass wardrobe"),
  R("Common bedroom","Wheat Oak Desk Cabin","common-bedroom-wheat-oak-desk-cabin","48% 50%","A platform bed with drawers, a pale wheat-oak wardrobe with ochre accent doors, and a wall-to-wall study desk with open knee space under the window.","Wheat Oak Desk Cabin common bedroom concept for Coastal Cabana with a platform bed and drawers, a wheat-oak wardrobe with ochre doors, and a wall-to-wall study desk with knee space")],
